{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cindery-charcoal-urubu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Target\n`src/rebar/_config_sources.py` — **791 LOC** on origin/main @ 059d54b725, against the 800-LOC hard\ncap. Nine lines of headroom, inside the gate's `>= 720` near-cap warning band.\n\n## Why this is filed late\nIt was excluded from this epic's original scope on 2026-08-19 because in-flight work owned the file\n(`masonic-abeyant-stagbeetle`, the P1 root-disk RCA). That ticket has since CLOSED, so nothing\nclaims the file today and it is the only near-cap file in the band with no owner. Re-measure before\nplanning: main moved substantially during this epic.\n\n## How to do it\nRead the file and derive the seam from the CALL GRAPH. `_config_sources.py` sits below the config\nseam that RP-04 spent several stories establishing, so respect that boundary — this is a split\nalong an existing concern, not a re-architecture of config ownership.\n\n## Constraints (inherited from the epic — all non-negotiable)\n- Split along LOGICAL CONCERNS / ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARIES, never mechanically. NAME the boundary in\n  the commit message and say why the call graph supports it.\n- NEVER raise the limit; `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is locked.\n- No resulting file under 100 LOC; target 200-500 each. Leave REAL headroom.\n- Behaviour-preserving: existing tests for this area pass UNMODIFIED.\n\n## Lessons from the five splits that landed before this one — apply all of them\n1. **Check both sides of the binding.** What monkeypatches the symbols you MOVE, and what\n   monkeypatches the symbols your moved code CALLS. The `config.py` split (Gerrit 1932) caused a\n   real behaviour change this way: a test patched `config.repo_root`, the moved function rebound it\n   from its new sibling at import time, and the code wrote outside the tmp root. Resolve such names\n   through the composition root at call time.\n2. **Update path-keyed registries in the same change.** Allowlists, line budgets, ownership\n   registries, golden files, census tests and `<file>:<line>` doc citations. Several live INSIDE\n   test files. `docs/env-vars.md` is CI drift-gated and records `<file>:<line>` for non-literal\n   `os.environ.get` reads — a config-adjacent split is very likely to shift those; regenerate.\n3. **Two complexity-baseline traps.** The baseline is keyed `<path>::<symbol>`. MOVING a baselined\n   symbol adds a key (`new>0`, CI fails). REDUCING complexity inside one makes it stale — which\n   PASSES `make lint` and FAILS CI. Run `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n   directly and require `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`. Never edit the baseline file.\n4. **Validate against the whole tree.** CI runs everything; two agents were caught by failures in\n   `tests/interfaces` after validating only `tests/unit`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_config_sources.py` is under the cap with REAL headroom, and every new file is\n      >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] The split follows an existing call-graph seam; the commit message names the concern boundary.\n- [ ] Behaviour unchanged: existing tests covering this area pass UNMODIFIED, including any test\n      that monkeypatches a symbol this module defines OR calls.\n- [ ] The public import surface is unchanged: no symbol previously resolvable through\n      `rebar._config_sources` stops resolving. Proven by comparing `dir()` against pre-split main.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`,\n      and `.github/module-size-limit.txt` and `.github/complexity-baseline.json` are unmodified.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass, and any CI drift-gated generated artifact\n      (e.g. `docs/env-vars.md`) is regenerated in the same change.","id":"1a33-8b6a-5bf2-4ab6","parent_id":"9224-5753-c3a9-4c33","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Split src/rebar/_config_sources.py (791 LOC) along its concern boundary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787189576696551001,"uuid":"06cfac8d-e536-4565-bc68-ac1d09c500af"}